  "id": "GHSA-6r6f-x5h8-fw8h",
  "details": "ImageMagick has a define `filename:literal=true` that can be used to treat filenames with percent signs (%) as plain text rather than formatting placeholders. To make it more easy to configure this the following security policy has been added:\r\n\r\n```xml\r\n  \u003c!-- Treat filenames with percent signs (%) as plain text rather than\r\n       formatting placeholders. --\u003e\r\n  \u003cpolicy domain=\"system\" name=\"filename:literal\" value=\"true\"/\u003e\r\n```",
